# Sandbox workshop context

You are editing **workshop-app** inside a Docker Sandbox (`sbx`).

## Platform split

| Repo | Role |
|------|------|
| **workshop-app** (this workspace) | Next.js playground — home, about, quick start; links to hosted platform |
| **Hosted platform** | Register, login, lab progress, Q&A — https://nextjs-26f1-3000.prg1.zerops.app |

Do not add Supabase or auth to workshop-app. Link outward via `NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_URL` (defaults in `src/lib/site-config.ts`).

## sbx basics

- Workspace syncs from the host — direct mode edits appear on the host immediately
- Clone mode (`--clone`) — agent commits in a private clone; host fetches `sandbox-<name>`
- Secrets stay on the host — VM sees sentinels; proxy injects real credentials
- Network is deny-by-default — kit allow-list permits npm, GitHub, etc.
